1
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:14,310
A garden has a flower bed shaped like a parallelogram, and a lawn shaped like a trapezium.

2
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:18,690
A trapezium has two parallel sides of different lengths.

3
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:23,570
Can we find their areas using only rectangles and triangles?

4
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:27,030
A parallelogram can be rearranged into which shape?

5
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:30,270
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:36,440
Cut a right-angled triangle off one end of the parallelogram, and slide it to the other end.

7
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:40,410
You get a rectangle, with the same base and height.

8
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:44,410
Remember: the area of a rectangle is length times width.

9
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:48,620
The area of a triangle is a half, times base, times height.

10
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:52,590
A triangle with base 8 and height 5 has area 20.

11
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:57,870
So the area of a parallelogram is base times height, just like the rectangle.

12
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:02,880
The height must be the perpendicular height, at right angles to the base.

13
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:04,940
Not the slanting side.

14
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:05,660
Your turn.

15
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:08,550
A parallelogram has base 7 and height 3.

16
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:09,780
What is its area?

17
00:01:09,830 --> 00:01:13,120
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:14,290
7 times 3 is 21.

19
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,590
Now the trapezium.

20
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:21,770
Two identical trapezia, one turned upside down, fit together to make a parallelogram.

21
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:25,370
Its base is a plus b, and its height is h.

22
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:27,610
So one trapezium is half of that.

23
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:32,110
Add the parallel sides, halve, and multiply by the height.

24
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,440
Here is the method.

25
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:39,240
Step 1: find the base, or the parallel sides, and the perpendicular height.

26
00:01:39,290 --> 00:01:42,260
Step 2: ignore any slanting sides.

27
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:47,410
Step 3: use A equals b h, or A equals a half, a plus b, times h.

28
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:50,390
Step 4: give the units squared.

29
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:57,130
A trapezium has parallel sides 6 and 10 centimetres, and height 5 centimetres.

30
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:03,990
6 plus 10 is 16, half of 16 is 8, and 8 times 5 is 40 square centimetres.

31
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:04,720
Your turn.

32
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:08,610
A trapezium has parallel sides 5 and 7, and height 2.

33
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:09,860
What is its area?

34
00:02:09,910 --> 00:02:12,870
Pause and work it out.

35
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,510
5 plus 7 is 12.

36
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,270
Half of 12 is 6.

37
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,580
6 times 2 is 12.

38
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:25,380
A trapezium has area 63 square centimetres, height 7, and one parallel side of 4.

39
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,650
Find the other.

40
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:29,670
63 equals a half, 4 plus b, times 7.

41
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:34,090
Half of 7 is 3.5, and 63 divided by 3.5 is 18.

42
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:36,700
So b is 14 centimetres.

43
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:41,460
A parallelogram has base 10, a slanting side of 6, and height 5.

44
00:02:41,510 --> 00:02:42,870
Max finds the area.

45
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,910
Which line is wrong?

46
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,070
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,960
He used the slanting side.

48
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:50,610
Use the perpendicular height.

49
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:54,680
10 times 5 is 50 square centimetres.

50
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:57,410
Many roofs have trapezium-shaped sides.

51
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:02,720
To order roof tiles, a builder works out the area of each trapezium.

52
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:14,890
A roof face with parallel edges of 8 and 12 metres, and a slope height of 4 metres, has an area of a half times 20 times 4, which is 40 square metres.

53
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,240
One last question.

54
00:03:16,290 --> 00:03:19,170
A parallelogram has area 40 and base 8.

55
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,600
What is its height?

56
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:24,030
Pause the video and answer.

57
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,820
40 equals 8 times h.

58
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:29,590
So h is 40 divided by 8, which is 5.

59
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:34,320
To remember: the area of a parallelogram is base times height.

60
00:03:34,370 --> 00:03:38,170
The area of a trapezium is a half, a plus b, times h.

61
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:41,250
Always use the perpendicular height.

62
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,180
Rearrange to find a missing length.

63
00:03:44,230 --> 00:03:49,550
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.2 on Camday.
